Phase OS-16: Kernel Filesystem Enhancements - 3 new AArch64 assembly kernel modules:

1. kernel/fs_journal.asm (Journaling Filesystem Support)
   - Base ID: 910
   - Journaling support for crash-consistent filesystem operations
   - Features: journal area management, transaction logging, commit/replay operations, checkpoint management, journal recovery after crash, synchronous/asynchronous journaling, journal statistics, multiple journal modes (ordered, writeback, data)
   - Data structures: journal_t (dev_id, start_block, num_blocks, transaction_id, commit_block, checkpoint, mode, active), journal_transaction_t (id, start_time, block_count, state, checksum)
   - API: fs_journal_init, fs_journal_create, fs_journal_start_transaction, fs_journal_add_block, fs_journal_commit, fs_journal_checkpoint, fs_journal_replay, fs_journal_stats
   - Capacity: 8 journals, 1024 transactions per journal, 4KB per block
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style (stp/ldp frame, .global exports, .bss for state)

2. kernel/fs_quota.asm (Filesystem Quotas)
   - Base ID: 911
   - User and group disk quota management
   - Features: user quota tracking, group quota tracking, quota limits (soft/hard), grace period management, quota enforcement, quota reporting, quota initialization per filesystem, quota warnings
   - Data structures: quota_entry_t (uid/gid, blocks_used, blocks_soft, blocks_hard, inodes_used, inodes_soft, inodes_hard, grace_start, warnings), quota_policy_t (fs_id, default_soft, default_hard, grace_period)
   - API: fs_quota_init, fs_quota_enable, fs_quota_disable, fs_quota_set_limits, fs_quota_update_usage, fs_quota_check, fs_quota_report, fs_quota_grace_check
   - Capacity: 256 user quotas, 128 group quotas per filesystem, 16 filesystems
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

3. kernel/fs_compress.asm (Filesystem Compression)
   - Base ID: 912
   - Transparent filesystem compression for storage efficiency
   - Features: block-level compression, compression algorithm selection (LZ4, LZO simplified), compression ratio tracking, decompression on read, compression on write, compression statistics, per-file compression flags, compression cache
   - Data structures: compress_entry_t (block_num, compressed_size, original_size, algorithm, checksum, cached), compress_stats_t (compressed_blocks, total_saved, ratio_avg, algorithm_counts)
   - API: fs_compress_init, fs_compress_block, fs_decompress_block, fs_compress_set_algo, fs_compress_stats, fs_compress_cache_add, fs_compress_cache_flush, fs_compress_ratio
   - Capacity: 4096 compressed blocks, 512 cache entries, 4 algorithms
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

Build all 3 kernel modules with:
  clang --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -c -O2 -o kernel/<name>.o kernel/<name>.asm

